{
  "_description": "Gold annotations for the 25-document parser-development sample. Each annotation is a reviewed, non-overlapping amendment instruction. These are used as ground truth for precision/recall/F1 computation. An instruction is identified by (target_ref, instruction_type). target_ref is normalized (whitespace-collapsed, lowercased) for matching.",
  "_methodology": "Each document was manually reviewed to identify all amendment instructions in the amendment body. Instructions are non-overlapping: one legal operation = one annotation. Container phrases like 'amended as follows' are NOT annotated separately when they contain sub-instructions; only the actual operations (add/delete/restate/replace) are annotated. Cross-references and amendment section headings are NOT annotated. Each annotation has a unique id and source_span [start, end] pointing to the instruction text in the source document. Matching uses annotation IDs and span overlap, not just (target_ref, instruction_type) keys. Each annotation has a unique id and source_span [start, end] pointing to the instruction text in the source document. Matching uses annotation IDs and span overlap, not just (target_ref, instruction_type) keys.",
